# Continue Implementation: Rules-Workflow Enhancement Protocol

## File Purpose and Relationship

This file defines the protocol for continuing a rules-workflow enhancement implementation from within the rules-workflow. It should be used when:

- Continuing implementation of rules-workflow documentation enhancements
- Resuming a rules-workflow documentation enhancement after interruption
- Maintaining implementation momentum for self-referential documentation
- Restoring context for rules-workflow documentation modifications
- Recovering from errors during rules-workflow enhancement implementation

This protocol ensures focused and consistent handling of rules-workflow enhancement implementations while maintaining proper self-referential boundaries and implementation continuity.

## Relation to Cognitive Architecture

This file is part of the rules-workflow knowledge component within the 1000xbrain cognitive architecture. It complements:

- `fetch_rules(["knowledge/patterns/impl/implementation-patterns"])`: Implementation patterns
- `@parameters/rules/dev-mode/dev-mode-rules-workflow-enhancement.mdc`: Rules-workflow enhancement protocol
- `@parameters/rules/plan-mode/plan-mode-rules-workflow-enhancement.mdc`: Planning guidance for rules-workflow enhancements
- `@parameters/rules/direct-mode/direct-mode-rules-workflow-enhancement.mdc`: Direct implementation without planning phase
- `fetch_rules(["knowledge/reference/guides/self-referential-workflow"])`: Self-referential workflow implementation guidelines

